<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bạch Đằng River</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bach Dang River</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bạch Đằng River is a tidal river in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> near Hạ Long Bay. It was the site of three famous Vietnamese victories: Ngô Quyền's defeat of the Southern Han fleet in 938, which ended a millennium of Chinese rule, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-dai-hanh">Lê Hoàn</a>'s defeat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> in 981, and Trần Hưng Đạo's destruction of a Mongol fleet in 1288, each using stakes planted in the riverbed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bach-dang-river.jpg" alt="Bạch Đằng River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Viethavvh at vi.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cua_song_Bach_Dang.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
